@name Leica Summilux-M 50mm f/1.4 ASPH - reconstruction
# RECONSTRUCTION, not manufacturer data (Leica publishes no prescription; the patent has no table).
# Geometry: circle/asphere fits to the vector lens cut in Leica's Feb-2023 data sheet, scaled to
# EFL 51.6 mm (0.281465 mm per PDF pt). nd/vd are fitted, not known (see NOTES.md). Asphere refit
# within ~2 um of the drawn profile. Semi-diameters = drawn element edges (mechanical); stop = drawn
# opening = paraxial f/1.40. Last thickness = polychromatic best focus at infinity (paraxial: 25.230).
#
# radius   thickness   material   semi-diameter
# 1: L1 front
    39.0842     5.3580   1.82467/42.03    18.577
# 2: L1 rear
    97.0547     0.2207   air              17.378
# 3: L2 front
    25.8075     7.7817   1.47335/87.33    16.269
# 4: L2/L3 cemented
   539.0222     3.1054   1.73639/35.17    15.269
# 5: L3 rear
    22.0556     5.5722   air              12.908
# 6: aperture stop
       stop     2.0007   air              12.604
# 7: L4 front (ASPHERIC)
  -124.9816     2.5546   1.75244/51.81    12.655   k=0 a4=-1.195732e-05 a6=-5.329680e-09
# asph k=0 A4=-1.195732e-05 A6=-5.329680e-09 A8=0 A10=0
# 8: L4 rear
  -233.1458     2.9545   air              12.660
# 9: L5' front
   -47.8096     3.1544   1.73750/29.58    12.655
# 10: L5'/L5 cemented
    66.0514     6.6102   1.90662/40.36    13.561
# 11: L5 rear (floating gap follows)
   -35.8474     0.5106   air              13.561
# focus-gap 11 inf=0.5106 close=1.7063 close_distance=0.70
# focus-gap 11 inf=0.5106 close=2.6424 close_distance=0.45
# 12: L6 front
    45.4566     6.4816   1.82569/46.46    12.556
# 13: L6/L7 cemented
   -44.0999     4.8465   1.57823/37.48    12.556
# 14: L7 rear
    30.0154    25.1984   air              12.860
# focus-gap 14 inf=25.1984 close=29.2016 close_distance=0.70
# focus-gap 14 inf=25.1984 close=32.3355 close_distance=0.45
#
# Focusing (patent DE102004008997 claim 8): the whole lens moves forward by e, the rear group L6/L7
# by 0.77*e (ratio measured from patent Fig. 2/2a; also the ratio minimising close-range spherical
# aberration here). e = 5.199 mm at 0.70 m (m = 1:11.3), e = 9.269 mm at 0.45 m (m = 1:6.4);
# close_distance in the focus-gap comments is measured from the image plane (Leica convention).
# @float below uses the parser's convention (object distance from the front vertex): 0.45 m from the
# image plane = 0.3644 m from the front vertex (0.6185 m for 0.70 m).
# The 0.45 m values extrapolate the 2004 floating law; Leica's 2023 cam may differ.
@float 11 0.5106 2.6424 0.3644
